WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.134
The House

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:01.768
Select Committee

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.269
investigating January six,

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.238
convening publicly one last time.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:08.008
He lost the 2020 election and knew it

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.776
in the end.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.978
He summoned the mob to Washington

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:16.016
and knowingly they were armed and angry.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:17.884
Pointed them to the Capitol

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:20.553
and told them to fight like hell.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:22.922
And laying out its case

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:23.790
that former President

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.859
Donald Trump was ultimately responsible

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:28.194
for the attack on the U.S. Capitol.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:31.164
No man who would behave that way

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:33.500
at that moment in time

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.467
can ever serve

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.468
in any position

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.871
of authority in our nation again.

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:41.174
He is unfit right for any office.

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:43.309
The committee referring multiple crimes

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.344
to the Justice Department

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.011
that they say

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.413
the former president committed while

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:48.148
trying to stay in the White House.

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:50.050
We believe that the evidence described

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.751
by my colleagues today

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:54.120
and assembled throughout our hearings

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.756
warrants a criminal referral

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.859
of former President Donald J.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:00.827
Trump,

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:01.961
including assisting

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.897
or aiding an insurrection, conspiracy

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.265
to defraud the United States,

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:07.333
obstruction of an official proceeding,

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.769
and conspiracy to make false statements.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.671
It believes there is sufficient evidence

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.806
for two others

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:15.041
conspiracy to injure or impede an officer

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.709
and seditious conspiracy.

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.178
The panel also referenced

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:18.978
Attorney and Trump

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:22.082
ally John Eastman to DOJ, but saying DOJ

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:22.949
will have to determine

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:25.318
who else should face prosecution.

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:26.219
Our understanding

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:28.288
of the role of many individuals

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:30.423
may be incomplete even today

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.658
because they refuse

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:33.593
to answer our questions.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.762
We trust that the Department of Justice

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.163
will be able to form

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.332
a far more complete picture.

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:40.500
Republican lawmakers

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.968
who snubbed committee subpoenas

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.670
referred to the House Ethics Committee

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:45.905
after 17

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:46.239
months of

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.907
investigating and roughly a thousand

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:48.975
witness interviews.

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.410
The committee determined that Trump

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.744
knew the fraud allegations

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.246
he was pushing were false,

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.381
but continued to amplify them anyway.

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.150
The committee has evidence

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.451
that ex-President Trump

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.420
planned to declare victory

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.555
and unlawfully to call for the vote

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.890
counting to stop,

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.092
and that he told numerous allies

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:07.727
about his intent

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.829
in the weeks before the election.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.364
Up say a couple of months.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.799
Even as some of Trump's closest

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:13.733
allies, like Hope

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.001
Hicks, worry the bogus

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.970
fraud claims were damaging his legacy.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.505
Trump persisted

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:20.940
He said something along the lines of,

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:21.808
You know,

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.810
nobody will care about my legacy

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.146
if I lose

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.850
so that won't matter.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.453
The only thing that matters is,

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.754
is winning.

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:35.855
Trump worked on a scheme

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:36.556
to transmit

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:37.790
false Electoral College

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:38.791
ballots and replace

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.827
Department of Justice leadership with one

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:41.928
that would do his bidding,

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:44.130
even pressuring his own vice president.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.632
President Trump

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:48.234
spearheaded an unprecedented campaign

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.603
to coerce him to do it anyway,

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.338
ultimately culminating

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.274
in a dangerous threat to Mr.

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:55.175
Pence's life.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.643
On January six,

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:57.143
the committee

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.278
also highlighting Trump's

00:02:58.278 --> 00:03:01.047
$250 million fundraising haul

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:02.215
between the election

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.750
and January six

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.951
raised primarily off

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.119
claims of election fraud

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:07.687
that did not exist.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.355
Questioning whether any of the money

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.823
was used to pay lawyers

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.325
who may have tried to obstruct

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:14.160
the congressional investigation

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.162
and evidence from one unnamed witness

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:18.331
who was urged to stay loyal to Trump.

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.200
The witness believed

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.067
this was an effort

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.502
to effect her testimony.

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:24.270
And we are concerned

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.205
that these efforts

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:26.873
may have been a strategy

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.341
to prevent the committee

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:29.943
from finding the truth

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.380
DOJ may be

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.114
interested in

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.950
evidence the committee has to provide

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.650
if they do believe

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.085
there was some kind of obstruction.

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:41.120
But I think what we are already hearing

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:41.821
from witnesses,

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.556
including that lawyer from John Eastman,

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:43.823
is that

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:45.658
these referrals from the committee

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:46.926
are not legally binding.

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:47.994
They don't hold any more weight

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:49.896
than a referral from an American citizen.

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:50.930
The attorney from Eastman

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.365
also said that the committee

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.466
missed an opportunity

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.635
to make real legislative changes

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.471
by pursuing a pretend criminal case Jake.

00:03:58.605 --> 00:03:58.871
All right.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.206
Sara Murray on Capitol Hill for us.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:00.840
Thank you so much.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:01.941
Let's bring in January 6th

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:02.775
committee member,

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:03.943
Democratic Congresswoman

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.912
Elaine Luria of Virginia.

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.247
First, let me just get your response

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.915
to the attorney for Mr.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.617
Eastman saying that

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:11.651
these referrals carry

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:12.652
no more weight

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:14.387
than any other referral

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:15.722
from any other American citizen

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:17.590
and basically attacking the committee.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.057
Well,

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:19.359
I think this has been a standard practice

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:20.660
over the course of our investigation.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.861
And that people attempt

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.396
to attack the committee,

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:24.163
discredit the committee,

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:24.931
rather than focus on.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:25.832
The real issue here

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.033
is that we have a former president,

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.768
United States, who essentially attempted

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:30.336
to stay in office

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.005
after he lost an election.

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:33.373
There was also a comment

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:35.008
that Mike Pence made.

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:37.043
He attacked the partizan nature

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:38.011
of the committee, blah, blah, blah.

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:39.379
But the other thing that I thought was

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.881
interesting is this is how he spins it.

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.150
He said today,

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.251
look, as I wrote in my book,

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:45.585
I think the

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:46.886
president's actions and words

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.955
on January six were reckless.

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:50.223
But I don't know that

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:50.723
it's criminal

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:53.526
to take bad advice from lawyers.

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:55.895
What do you what do you make of that?

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:56.296
Well,

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:57.830
I'm actually kind of tired of Mike Pence

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.033
trying to have it both ways. He really

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.101
takes the limelight

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:02.435
and likes

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:03.803
to be portrayed as a hero who

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:04.671
because he did

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:05.872
his job and followed the law,

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:06.739
but at the same time

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:09.409
then goes back and tries to attack

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.311
a committee that is bipartisan.

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:11.711
Really, it's

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:13.646
been one of those bipartisan committees

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:14.213
in the House.

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:14.514
And the way

00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:15.148
we've worked together

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:16.182
and presented the evidence

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:18.518
and the facts are the facts

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:21.020
and he has tried to discredit it

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:21.954
in the public sphere.

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:24.290
Many have tried to undermine the

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:25.358
nature of the composition

00:05:25.358 --> 00:05:26.392
of the committee through the courts.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:26.793
And the courts

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:27.894
have clearly rejected that.

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:28.795
The truth is, is

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:29.462
we did our job

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.363
as a congressional committee.

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:31.064
As for oversight

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:32.398
and legislation, we've laid out

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:33.066
the facts.

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:34.367
We've painted a very clear picture

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:35.935
for the American people of what led up to

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:36.869
and happened on that day.

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:38.471
It's spelled out in our report

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:39.872
the executive summary is out today.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:40.573
Later this week,

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.475
the full comprehensive report

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:43.176
will be out, along

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:44.610
with all of the testimony

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.478
in the executive summary.

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:46.846
Look at the witnesses we have in there.

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:47.246
You know, nine

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:48.614
9% of them are Republicans

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:49.949
who served in the Trump administration.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:51.784
And many of them were appointed

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:54.153
by Trump himself and performed by

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:55.621
his Republican Senate.

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:56.189
And those are the people

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:57.190
who had the courage to come forward

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.991
and speak and talk about the facts

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.460
So, you know, people who continue

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.528
to evade the questions of the committee

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:04.731
and try to undermine the committee

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:06.165
as a committee within Congress,

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:07.967
you know, they you know, Mr.

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:09.135
Eastman's lawyer said, you know,

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:10.937
it wasn't worth any more than,

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:11.704
you know,

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:13.439
potentially any citizen saying it.

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:15.007
You know, they're

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:16.476
you know, it's kind of it's hot air.

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:17.844
It's deflection.

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:18.611
I think and,

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:18.811
you know,

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:19.879
we get back to the point is

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:22.081
all of this should be focused on

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:22.882
the facts.

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.450
And we laid that out today

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.252
and our referrals.

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:26.552
It's true

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:27.720
that they don't carry the weight of law

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:28.888
and it's also true,

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:29.889
and I've said this early on,

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:30.990
I mean, the attorney general,

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:31.424
you know, Mr.

00:06:31.424 --> 00:06:32.992
Garland, you don't have to wait for us.

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:33.693
And they haven't

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:34.560
they've been running

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.762
with this investigation.

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:36.396
And, you know,

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:37.997
since we're not coordinating our efforts,

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:38.598
their efforts,

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:39.332
you know, I've looked at this

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:41.367
like a relay with a passing off a baton.

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:42.368
The runner receiving

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:43.836
the baton is already running, you know,

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:45.204
and they've got to keep going with it.

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:46.205
So I think we've

00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:46.539
you know,

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:47.640
our committee is coming to an end

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:48.674
because the end of this Congress,

00:06:48.674 --> 00:06:49.675
we've issued a report

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:51.077
and we've passed this off

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:52.111
to the Department of Justice

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:53.746
with the full information we've gathered.

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:55.848
And we recommend that they look

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:57.417
at criminal activity of the people

00:06:57.417 --> 00:06:58.718
starting at the top.

00:06:58.718 --> 00:06:59.986
Trump, former President Trump.

00:06:59.986 --> 00:07:02.255
So I know that the committee was

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:03.356
the select committee was only

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:04.957
formed for this one Congress,

00:07:06.025 --> 00:07:08.394
but I also know that,

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:08.995
you know, midterm

00:07:08.995 --> 00:07:09.962
elections generally

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:12.365
swing the way this one swung.

00:07:12.365 --> 00:07:15.601
And, you know, Kevin McCarthy or whoever

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.336
the Republican speaker becomes

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:18.504
was going to kill the committee

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:20.273
even if it had been put in there

00:07:20.273 --> 00:07:21.841
for for more than one term.

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:22.341
And I'm wondering

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:24.444
if you felt like you had enough time

00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:27.313
and resources to investigate

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:28.681
everything you wanted to

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:32.018
when it came to the insurrection?

00:07:32.018 --> 00:07:33.453
I think that we did

00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:34.787
a comprehensive investigation

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:36.122
talking to a thousand

00:07:36.122 --> 00:07:37.824
that this is roughly

00:07:37.824 --> 00:07:39.358
hundreds of thousands of documents,

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:41.194
including a huge tranche of information

00:07:41.194 --> 00:07:42.361
from the Secret Service.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.763
I mean, this is not the end of this

00:07:43.763 --> 00:07:44.130
we look at.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:47.233
This is really the beginning in a sense.

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:48.534
You know,

00:07:48.534 --> 00:07:50.203
as we said in the hearing today

00:07:50.203 --> 00:07:51.237
for the Department of Justice

00:07:51.237 --> 00:07:52.138
to take the information

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:52.772
that we've gathered

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.240
along with what they've gathered.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.441
And the end of this is holding

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:56.042
people accountable

00:07:56.042 --> 00:07:56.742
and making sure like this,

00:07:56.742 --> 00:07:58.311
something like this doesn't happen again.

00:07:58.311 --> 00:07:58.711
So

00:07:59.779 --> 00:08:00.346
there's more to

00:08:00.346 --> 00:08:01.113
be done than

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:03.950
we had time and ultimately resources for.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:05.151
Do you think the January.

00:08:05.151 --> 00:08:05.718
Do you think

00:08:05.718 --> 00:08:07.353
the Justice Department

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:08.921
would have been as aggressive

00:08:08.921 --> 00:08:09.489
as they've been?

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:10.423
And I know there are a lot of people

00:08:10.423 --> 00:08:10.890
who think they haven't

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.091
been aggressive enough,

00:08:12.091 --> 00:08:13.559
but I mean, they did get guilty

00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:14.293
pleas for the Oath

00:08:14.293 --> 00:08:15.828
Keepers on seditious conspiracy.

00:08:15.828 --> 00:08:17.430
There have been other charges.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.232
And who knows what's going to come.

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:20.199
Do you think that they would have done

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:21.000
as much as they did

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.802
if it hadn't been for the January six

00:08:22.802 --> 00:08:24.103
committee kind of blazing a trail?

00:08:24.103 --> 00:08:26.372
And on that subject,

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:29.041
why shouldn't the Senate form now?

00:08:29.041 --> 00:08:30.877
The Democrats have 51 votes

00:08:30.877 --> 00:08:32.044
and they can form committees

00:08:32.044 --> 00:08:34.080
and have subpoena power, etc.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.114
Why shouldn't the Senate

00:08:35.114 --> 00:08:36.048
take up the stance now?

00:08:36.048 --> 00:08:37.383
They were attacked, too?

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:37.717
Well,

00:08:37.717 --> 00:08:38.985
as far as the Department of Justice,

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:39.418
I think

00:08:39.886 --> 00:08:40.887
it's a lot of speculation

00:08:40.887 --> 00:08:41.554
in some regards.

00:08:41.554 --> 00:08:42.889
I mean, we know the Department of Justice

00:08:42.889 --> 00:08:43.756
has been investigating.

00:08:43.756 --> 00:08:44.190
I would look it's

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:45.791
looked at as concentric circles.

00:08:45.791 --> 00:08:46.826
You know, it started on the outside.

00:08:46.826 --> 00:08:48.327
They started with the people who they had

00:08:48.327 --> 00:08:50.229
direct evidence of trespassing,

00:08:50.229 --> 00:08:50.696
you know,

00:08:50.696 --> 00:08:51.931
vandalism, you know,

00:08:51.931 --> 00:08:53.366
attacking police officers.

00:08:53.366 --> 00:08:53.866
And they were

00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:54.734
the 900

00:08:54.734 --> 00:08:56.235
people have been charged

00:08:56.235 --> 00:08:57.837
And we kind of started the center

00:08:57.837 --> 00:08:58.771
and worked our way out.

00:08:58.771 --> 00:08:59.772
So this is,

00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:00.406
I think, the point

00:09:00.406 --> 00:09:01.307
when those two concentric

00:09:01.307 --> 00:09:02.942
investigations of converge,

00:09:02.942 --> 00:09:03.743
we're passing it off

00:09:03.743 --> 00:09:04.677
to the Department of Justice.

00:09:04.677 --> 00:09:05.945
And I would like to see them

00:09:05.945 --> 00:09:07.146
go all the way to the top

00:09:07.146 --> 00:09:07.914
and hold those people

00:09:07.914 --> 00:09:08.915
in the highest levels

00:09:08.915 --> 00:09:10.583
of trust of the American people.

00:09:10.583 --> 00:09:11.584
As the former president

00:09:11.584 --> 00:09:13.719
and others who have failed to come

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:15.755
speak to the committee under subpoena

00:09:15.755 --> 00:09:17.223
to hold those people accountable

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:18.157
where applicable.

00:09:19.525 --> 00:09:20.259
And you know,

00:09:20.259 --> 00:09:21.460
the other thing about the Senate

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:22.495
is I certainly think, you know,

00:09:22.495 --> 00:09:22.895
the Senate

00:09:22.895 --> 00:09:24.330
having a Democratic majority

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.365
with 51 votes has the capability to take

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:27.466
especially the recommendations,

00:09:27.466 --> 00:09:28.734
the legislative recommendations

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:30.303
that we've laid out

00:09:30.303 --> 00:09:32.338
and move forward those inapplicable

00:09:32.338 --> 00:09:33.539
know committees of jurisdiction

00:09:33.539 --> 00:09:35.274
to make sure that we can

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:36.609
actually act on them.

00:09:36.609 --> 00:09:37.843
I was always a concern of mine

00:09:37.843 --> 00:09:38.077
is, you know,

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:38.711
we can lay out

00:09:38.711 --> 00:09:39.645
what our recommendations

00:09:39.645 --> 00:09:40.680
are legislatively

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.683
to process wise within different agencies

00:09:43.683 --> 00:09:44.650
and departments in the government

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:45.051
to prevent

00:09:45.051 --> 00:09:46.919
something like this in the future,

00:09:46.919 --> 00:09:47.820
but not

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:49.121
holding the majority in the House

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:49.989
past these midterms.

00:09:49.989 --> 00:09:50.523
We know

00:09:50.523 --> 00:09:51.924
Kevin McCarthy, Jim Jordan,

00:09:51.924 --> 00:09:53.593
they want to come in

00:09:53.593 --> 00:09:54.860
the very people who didn't

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:56.295
comply with subpoenas for the House,

00:09:56.295 --> 00:09:57.897
want to be the speaker of the House,

00:09:57.897 --> 00:09:58.798
and they want to be the chair

00:09:58.798 --> 00:10:00.466
of the Judiciary Committee in the House.

00:10:00.466 --> 00:10:01.968
And they want to enforce subpoenas,

00:10:01.968 --> 00:10:03.603
but they wouldn't even answer themselves.

00:10:03.603 --> 00:10:05.137
And that how ironic is that?

